# .trufflehog-ignore — path-exclude file for TruffleHog (`--exclude-paths`).
#
# Format: one PATH REGEX per line (Go RE2 syntax). Blank lines and lines
# starting with `#` are ignored. Each pattern excludes matching file paths from
# the scan. Keep this list narrow — excluding whole trees can hide real secrets.
#
# For GRANULAR, per-finding suppression prefer an inline comment on the exact
# line instead of excluding a whole path:
#     const EXAMPLE_TOKEN = "AKIA...";  // trufflehog:ignore
# That keeps the rest of the file scanned and documents the false positive in
# place. Reserve this file for paths that are inherently all-noise.
#
# Fixture-SHAPED noise (UUIDv7 ids, `test-`/`fake-`-prefixed passwords,
# redaction output) is not a path problem: do not exclude `tests/` or
# `fixtures/` here. Mark the line inline, or — when Gitleaks also runs — add a
# shape regex to .gitleaks.toml (see templates/.gitleaks.toml.example and
# sec-01 §3 "Scanner False Positives on Test Fixtures").
#
# This file ships EMPTY on purpose. A path exclude drops every finding in the
# file whatever its value, so it is only right for a file that cannot carry a
# credential at all — and the usual candidates can:
#   - lockfiles (`package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock`, `Cargo.lock`, …) carry the
#     registry URLs the package manager wrote, token and all, when someone
#     installed from a private URL; their hash noise is for the detector's own
#     verification/entropy filters, not a path exclude;
#   - committed bundles (`dist/`, `*.min.js`) are where a build-time-injected
#     credential lands;
#   - `tests/`, `__tests__/`, `fixtures/`, `examples/` hold the fixtures the
#     inline marker and the Gitleaks shape allowlist exist for.
#
# Exclude a specific artifact only when it is provably credential-free, and
# name that artifact, never the tree (regexes, so `\.` escapes a dot):
#
# ^public/vendor/highlight\.min\.js$          # upstream build, no config injected
# ^assets/fonts/[^/]+\.(woff2?|ttf|eot)$      # binary font files in one directory
